{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrPcaZg75bgBPTQm9jir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't see the exact defect in the retrieved code. `UsersService.create` and the user persistence mapper aren't in the snippets, and they are the most likely place for it. My best candidate is `AuthService.register`, and this is a low-confidence diagnosis.\n\n`validateLogin` is behaving correctly. It returns `needLoginViaProvider:<provider>` only when the stored `user.provider` isn't `email`. So a freshly registered user must have been saved with `provider = 'google'`.\n\n`register` never sets `provider`. It spreads the raw `dto` into `usersService.create`, so the stored value depends on a default applied downstream, and a `provider` field in the request body could also be passed through.\n\n<function_calls>\n<invoke name=\"StructuredOutput\">\n<parameter name=\"candidates\">[{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"symbol\":\"AuthService.register\",\"start_line\":200,\"end_line\":211,\"explanation\":\"register creates the user by spreading the raw DTO and does not set provider to AuthProvidersEnum.email. The persisted provider therefore depends on a default in UsersService.create or the persistence mapper, which is not shown. A user saved with provider 'google' is rejected by validateLogin with needLoginViaProvider:google. A provider field in the request body would also be passed through.\"},{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"symbol\":\"AuthService.validateLogin\",\"start_line\":50,\"end_line\":54,\"explanation\":\"The login check rejects any user whose stored provider is not 'email'. It is correct, but it surfaces the wrong provider value that was stored at registration.\"}]</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"fix\">{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"description\":\"In AuthService.register, pass provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email explicitly to usersService.create, after the spread so a client-supplied value cannot override it. Also check UsersService.create and the user persistence mapper, and make sure any default provider is 'email' and not 'google'.\"}</parameter>\n</invoke>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":15183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56543ed3-0e03-44e3-9217-749f3daaaeb7","uuid":"e40a9fa9-6a38-44fe-ae4a-e13651b35329","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:15:41.991Z","request_id":"req_011CgrPcaHYkYxSBJey9gquy"}
